      "rev_n_22_0dd0f0_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_22_0dd0f0_0",
        "node_id": "n_22_0dd0f0",
        "thought_text": "Since the array is circular and n is divisible by k, the sequence of tasks Dima performs for a starting offset 's' consists of indices s, s+k, s+2k, ..., s+(n/k-1)k (all modulo n). We can precompute the sum for each of the k possible starting offsets (1 to k) by iterating through the array once with a step of k, then find the minimum sum and the smallest index achieving it.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5649633481775433972",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794589801.7302167
