      "rev_n_23_491061_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_23_491061_0",
        "node_id": "n_23_491061",
        "thought_text": "We can simulate the process for each potential starting position from 1 to k. For each start, we calculate the total 'telling off' power by summing the values at indices start, start+k, start+2k, etc., wrapping around using modulo arithmetic. We track the minimum total power found and the corresponding starting task number, ensuring we pick the smallest index in case of ties.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5649633481775433972",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794589801.7302325
      },
      "rev_n_24_400167_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_24_400167_0",
        "node_id": "n_24_400167",
        "thought_text": "Given the constraints (n up to 10^5), an O(n) approach is required. We can create k separate lists or accumulators where the i-th accumulator stores the sum of a[j] where j % k == i. After populating these, we simply find the index with the minimum sum. This avoids recalculating sums for overlapping sequences and ensures linear time complexity.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5649633481775433972",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
